+# Performance patch evaluation queue
+
+Snapshot: 2026-10-24. Initial shortlist, not an exhaustive inventory. All 18 PRs were open and unmerged when queried. Review states are evidence, not proof of correctness. No new hardware performance claim has been established locally.
+
+## One candidate at a time
+
+1. Read discussion and inline reviews, check license and exact source revision, then check upstream and fork ancestry for duplicates.
+2. Apply one candidate to a fixed baseline in its own branch. Build and run relevant correctness tests before hardware measurement.
+3. Run baseline/candidate/candidate/baseline with identical models, prompts, placement, cache budget, KV types, affinity, compiler and ROCm. Keep individual samples, logs and source/build IDs. Use at least three measured repetitions and separate cold from warm cache results.
+4. Check output correctness, PP, TG, memory use, speculative acceptance, and short-prompt regressions. Retain only reproducible benefits for the intended workload. Approximation or quant changes require separate quality evaluation.
+5. Merge an accepted candidate into the experimental integration branch. Test the next patch against that accepted revision. A rejected candidate must not remain in the next baseline.
+
+## First experiment
+
+Baseline: amd-main `e3f526dd7`. Candidate: `experimental/perf-29963` at `04587fd2f`, containing only PR 29963 and conflict resolution. It excludes provisional MXFP4 batching and pinned staging.
+
+Use the same four-GPU layer split, disable automatic fitting initially, and test its changed fitting policy separately. Test DeepSeek and GLM with real identical prompts at 512, 8192 and 32768 tokens and 256-token generation. Start without speculation, then test DSpark/MTP at intended production settings. Compare cache off and the same known-fitting cache budget on both builds. Confirm pipeline activation in candidate logs. Record exact input/output token counts and save generated content.
+
+The user runs hardware tests on Galactus; no SSH is authorized. Local CPU builds and allocator tests do not validate HIP stream correctness or performance. Do not stack the next candidate while this result is pending.
+
